From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jason chien <3936511+jason5545@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 20:04:58 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] kk: lighter encoder end barriers, opt-in unchecked
 constant buffers

From Highball (highball-engine, kosmickrisp-arm64/highball/0007-encoder-barriers-and-constant-buffers.patch at
34bd3b0, 2026-11-04), written there with an LLM's help. Two hunks placed by hand, the code is Highball's: the u_debug.h include goes after nir_to_msl.h (which fxgl/steamac v1.9.7 adds), and null_ubo is freed before vk_pipeline_cache_destroy, which steamac 0055 moved there. This changes a default: an encoder's end barrier asks for Device visibility instead of ResourceAlias unless a render encoder ran an occlusion query; HB_KK_ALIAS_BARRIERS=1 brings the old barrier back. HB_KK_NO_UBO_ROBUST=1 stays off unless set.

Highball's README: GPU time 26.7 to 24.4 ms in Forza Horizon 6's benchmark on a base M4; HB_KK_NO_UBO_ROBUST=1 drops the bounds check on constant buffer reads, 24.4 to 21 ms there.

Applies after 0010.
